<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/talks-ted-ai> {
 ex:ted-scene-ai a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:ted-ai-orchestration ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ted-ai-heading, ex:ted-ai-diagram, ex:ted-ai-bullets ; cd:narration "Add a planning layer for Laboratory 5.0. Standardized interfaces make our registered processing operations discoverable and callable through an MCP server. MCP means Model Context Protocol. An AI agent can inspect names, definitions, ports and constraints, compose an explicit graph and submit it for validation. This is useful when many steps and branches make manual workflow construction cumbersome. The inspected source exposes a service-call gateway with semantic discovery and validation; the diagram does not claim a separately enumerated MCP tool for every step. Keep planning and execution distinct: the agent proposes the plan, validation checks it, and the execution engine runs the saved graph. Reproducible deterministic execution depends on suitable implementations and fixed data, parameters, software versions and seeds where needed. The same controls constrain invented calls but do not eliminate hallucinations or prove that a chosen analytical workflow is scientifically appropriate. Retain domain review, permissions, failure handling and result checks. This is the speaker-described capability and architecture, not an autonomous TED-method validation or an effectiveness claim."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ted-ai-orchestration ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-diagram a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ted-ai-flow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
